<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Analyzing Factory B's Wastage Rate and Workforce Management</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The wastage rate in factory \(B\) has been found to be as follows.</p>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="50%", style="text-align:center">Year</th>
    <th width="50%", style="text-align:center">Factory \(B\)</th>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(0\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y0@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(1\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y1@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(2\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y2@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(3\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y3@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(4\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y4@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(5\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y5@}\)</td>
    </tr>
 <tr>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\(6\)</td>
    <td width="50%", style="text-align:center">\({@wst_rt_y6@}\)</td>
    </tr>
</table>
</p>
<p>Calculate the average length of service of an employee and the annual intake required to maintain the staff at \({@no_of_staff@}\) persons.</p>
<p><b>Note: </b> <b>Compute the answer using a life table with a radix of 1000; round off the values in your table to the nearest integer.</b></p>
<p>a) The average length of service of an employee \(=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]\(years\)  <b>(Give your answer correct to 3 decimal places)</b></p>
<p>b) The annual intake required to maintain the staff at \({@no_of_staff@}\) persons \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]] \(persons\) <b>(Give your answer to the nearest whole number)</b></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution </h3>
<p>Always assume the radix of  \(l_0=1000\) and that withdrawals are uniformly spread over the year.</p>
<p>For factory \(B\), we have:</p>
<p>\(d_x = l_x * q_x\): this is the number of deaths between ages \(x\) and \(x+1\).</p>
<p>\(l_{x+1} = l_x - d_x\): this is the number of survivors to exact age \(x\).</p>
<p> \(L_x =\frac{l_{x+1}+l_x}{2}\): this is the number of persons now alive (present in the factory) and aged (has worked) between \(x\) and \(x+1\) years exactly (also called survivors between \(x\) and \(x+1\)).</p>
<p>\(T_x = L_x + L_{x+1} + ...\): this is the total number of person years lived between ages \(x\) and \(x+n\).</p>
<p></p>
<p>Therefore, the total number of years lived between each age interval is:</p>
<p>\(L_0 + L_1 + L_2 + L_3 +………..+L_n = T_0\)</p>
<p> Similarly,</p>
<p>\( T_x = L_x + L_{x+1} + L_{x+2} +…………+  L_{x+n}\)</p>
<p>\(T_x = L_x + T_{x+1} \) hence, \(T_x\) is also known as the number of persons aged \(x\) and over in a stationary population.</p>
<p>We can also write \(T_x\) as follows;</p>
<p>\(T_x =\sum_{i=1}^n\) and so, \(T_x\) can also mean the life table total population.</p>
<p>(withdrawals are taken to be deaths)</p>
<p>For factory \(B\), we have:</p>
